Package: daltonr
Type: Package
Title: Modern CVD-Friendly 'ggplot2' Theme with Crameri, Viridis, Cividis and Petroff Palettes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jian Wei", "Cheong", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "contact@jianwei.simplelogin.com")
Description: Provides 'theme_daltonr()', a 'ggplot2' theme in the modern
    scientific style that sets CVD-friendly default colour scales. Discrete
    aesthetics automatically use the qualitative Petroff colour palettes
    (petroff6, petroff8, petroff10, picked based on the number of groups), and
    continuous aesthetics use the scientific colour maps of Fabio Crameri or
    viridis/cividis. Scale functions are provided for every colour map, on both
    continuous and discrete scales. 'theme_daltonr()' adds automatic linetypes
    to discrete-colour line plots, makes raster and filled-contour plots fill
    the axis frame, and styles matplotlib-like colourbars.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: ggplot2 (>= 3.5.0), grDevices, rlang, scales
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
